# ── THE LOOP SAFETY CEILING (NOT a goal) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ REFRAMED 2026-07-30 (owner): this number is a BACKSTOP, not a target. The real terminal
# condition of the autonomous loop is the PHASE CERTIFICATES (Phase-0 cert → v1.0.0 → … → Phase-6),
# handled by the standing triggers — NOT an arbitrary tick count. Reaching a tick number says
# nothing about whether any phase is done, so the loop must NOT treat hitting this as "complete."
#
# Behaviour when TICK reaches this ceiling (loop-forever.sh): the supervisor PAUSES with a loud,
# recurring alarm and RE-CHECKS — it does NOT exit and does NOT claim completion. Raising the number
# (edit here or ./scripts/autoloop.sh set <K>) auto-resumes it; no restart needed. To actually STOP
# the loop, use the kill file:  touch .git/manuk-loop-DISABLED  (or pkill -f loop-forever.sh).
#
# Set FAR above any realistic phase-completion tick so it never interrupts mid-phase; it exists only
# so an unattended, cost-bearing, auto-respawning loop is never truly unbounded (this loop has OOMed
# the box and double-spawned when uncapped). 5000 = ~4200 ticks of headroom from t749, well past the
# whole Phase 0→6 journey; raise it if a phase ever legitimately approaches it.
LOOP_UNTIL_TICK=5000
